  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U-LEAD SALAR Support to the Roll-out Phase 2018-2020 - U-LEAD SALAR Support to the Roll-out Phase 2018-2020 VAT</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">U-LEAD SKR st&#xf6;d till roll-out fasen 2018-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For the Roll-out phase of U-LEAD, Sida will procure implementing partners to support the establishment of up to 575 administrative service centres. This contribution is about SALAR&apos;s role to select feasible local authorities and together with them work out a programme for how the establishment of the administrative service centre should be carried out in each local authority. This will be executed in four batches, with around 150 local authorities in each batch. SALAR will also work with policy support, methods support, peer review and exchange between administrative service centers and be responsible for coordination and implementation of communication and visibility in Sida&apos;s U-LEAD programme.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">F&#xf6;r Roll-out fasen av U-LEAD kommer Sida att handla upp implementerande partners f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja etablerandet av upp till 575 administrativa service centran i Ukraina. Denna insats avser att SKL ska arbeta med att v&#xe4;lja ut l&#xe4;mpliga kommuner och tillsammans med dessa arbeta fram ett underlag f&#xf6;r hur etableringen av det administrativa service centrat ska g&#xe5; till i respektive kommun. Detta kommer att ske i fyra omg&#xe5;ngar, med cirka 150 kommuner i varje omg&#xe5;ng. Dessutom kommer SKL i denna insats arbeta med policyr&#xe5;dgivning, metodst&#xf6;d, utbyte mellan etablerade administrativa service center och med att samordna och &#xf6;vergripande ansvara f&#xf6;r kommunikation och synlighet inom Sidas U-LEAD program.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U-LEAD with Europe contributes to the implementation of the Decentralization Reform in Ukraine. Component 2 on &quot;Support to Improved Administrative Service Delivery&quot;, coordinated by Sida, aims at establishment of up to 600 Administrative Service Centres, as well as development IT systems (Trembita and Vulyk) for efficient e-governance that will enable safe and secure delivery of Government-to-Government, Government-to-Business and Government-to- Citizens public and administrative services at the central, regional and local levels.</narrative>
  </description>
